"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n4.8 dev 7 (The feature was only recently added in this version)\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.8.dev7 - Windows 11 (build 26200) - Multi-window, 1 monitor (1920x1080 @ 59.98 Hz) - Direct3D 12 (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce GTX 1050 (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.8278) - Intel(R) Core(TM) i5-8300H CPU @ 2.30GHz (8 threads) - 11.85 GiB memory - WASAPI (48000 Hz, Stereo/mono)\n\n### Issue description\n\nThe newly added event sounds for control themes accept AudioStream (and the classes inheriting it). It works as expected until assigning an AudioStreamRandomizer resource (with at least one stream) where the audio wont play at all.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nAssign a custom theme (or use Theme Overrides) with a sound to an event (in this case, pressed) with value of an AudioStreamRandomizer resource with at least one stream and run the project and try to listen to the sound after playing the event.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[audio-rand-theme-bug.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/33011007/audio-rand-theme-bug.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Re